  "sources": [
    {
      "number": "425",
      "solution": "a: arrows 1->20,2->30,3->40,4->50,5->50; inverse 20->1,30->2,40->3,50->4,50->5. D={1,2,3,4,5}, R={20,30,40,50}; inverse domain/range swap. b: arrows 1/2->3,1/3->4,2/3->5,1/4->5,3/4->7; inverse 3->1/2,4->1/3,5->2/3,5->1/4,7->3/4. D={1/2,1/3,2/3,1/4,3/4}, R={3,4,5,7}; inverse swaps these sets. Each repeated output must retain both reversed arrows."
    },
    {
      "number": "426",
      "solution": "a inverse={(7,sqrt2),(8,sqrt3),(10,sqrt5),(11,sqrt6),(12,sqrt7)}; original domain={sqrt2,sqrt3,sqrt5,sqrt6,sqrt7}, range={7,8,10,11,12}. b inverse={(1,0.3),(0,sqrt10),(1,-2),(0,sqrt6),(1,13)}; original domain={0.3,sqrt10,-2,sqrt6,13}, range={0,1}. c inverse={(12,1),(6,2),(4,3),(3,4),(2,6),(1,12)}, the same set as original; domain=range={1,2,3,4,6,12}. All inverse domains/ranges swap their originals; neither repeated 0 nor repeated 1 discards a pair."
    },
    {
      "number": "427",
      "solution": "For ordered arguments a,b the inverses are: a is south of b; a is younger than b; a is 2 less than b (a=b-2); a is five times b (a=5b, both positive). Swapping arguments reverses direction, not the sign or reciprocal of either argument."
    },
    {
      "number": "428",
      "solution": "Direct pixel tracing gives f={(-2,1),(-1,-1),(1,-2),(3,-1),(4,1)}. Plot these five isolated points; inverse={(1,-2),(-1,-1),(-2,1),(-1,3),(1,4)}, reflecting each point in y=x. f is a function because each left element has exactly one outgoing arrow. Its inverse is not: input -1 has outputs -1 and 3; input 1 has outputs -2 and 4.",
      "figure_owner": "428"
    },
    {
      "number": "429",
      "solution": "Known inverse points are (1,-8),(7,1),(9,0); any two distinct points suffice. The wording does not establish that these are all points of the relation."
    },
    {
      "number": "430",
      "solution": "Original closed segment joins (-3,2) to (4,5), y=(3x+23)/7 with -3<=x<=4. Inverse closed segment joins (2,-3) to (5,4), y=(7x-23)/3 with 2<=x<=5. Original D=[-3,4], R=[2,5]; inverse D=[2,5], R=[-3,4]. Lines without segment restrictions are not the full graph."
    },
    {
      "number": "431",
      "solution": "Upper semicircle lies on x^2+y^2=9 with y positive in its interior; reflecting in y=x gives the right semicircle with x positive in its interior. At x=1 the inverse has y=+sqrt8 and -sqrt8, so it is not a function regardless of endpoint membership. The prose does not settle whether original (+/-3,0), and hence inverse (0,+/-3), are included. Preserve that uncertainty; interior orientation and nonfunction verdict require no convention.",
      "endpoint_membership": "UNKNOWN; no closed/open half-plane convention inferred"
    },
    {
      "number": "432",
      "solution": "Inverse equations a y-5x=3; b y+3x=1; c y+x=5; d y^2-x=0; e 2y^2+5y=x-x^2; f yx=10; g y^2+x^2=9; h y^2-x^2=12; i y^2-x^2=0. Exactly c,f,g,i are self-inverse. For h swapping yields x^2-y^2=-12, not the original. For e (0,1) satisfies the original but not its inverse; rearrangement alone does not make it symmetric."
    },
    {
      "number": "433",
      "solution": "a original y=x/2-2, inverse y=2x+4 (or x- y/2=-2); inverse line through (0,4),(-2,0). b original y=3x/2-3, inverse y=2x/3+2; inverse through (0,2),(-3,0). c original y=x^2, inverse x=y^2: vertex (0,0), opens right, both branches y=+/-sqrt(x), x>=0. d original y=-(x-2)^2, inverse x=-(y-2)^2: vertex (0,2), opens left, both branches y=2+/-sqrt(-x), x<=0. All graphs reflect in y=x."
    },
    {
      "number": "434",
      "solution": "Over real variables: a numerator=(b+3)(b+5), denominator=(b+5)(b^2-5b+25), result (b+3)/(b^2-5b+25), b!=-5. b numerator=(p-7)(p-3), denominator=(3-p)(p^2+3p+9), result (7-p)/(p^2+3p+9), p!=3. c numerator=(x+1)(x^2-7x+19), denominator=(x+1)(x^2-x+1), result (x^2-7x+19)/(x^2-x+1), x!=-1. d numerator=(a+2)(a^2+a+1), denominator=(a-1)(a^2+a+1), result (a+2)/(a-1), a!=1. The quadratic factors have negative discriminants and introduce no further real exclusions."
    },
    {
      "number": "435",
      "solution": "a 8^-3*(1/2)^-10=2^-9*2^10=2. b 81^5*9^-11=3^20*3^-22=1/9. c 1.5^3*(3/8)^-1+(-1/3)^-1=(27/8)*(8/3)-3=9-3=6."
    }
  ],
